From 0d7263ac4e94bcc68cf643ecc5a9280b0af260fd Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: NeoTech <andreas@roughedge.se>
Date: Sun, 22 Nov 2026 14:20:40 +0100
Subject: [PATCH] fix(multiaxis): state the rotaries before the first tilted
 feed

A leaning 5-axis path left its opening moves without a pose, and the
dump commanded zero angles only after a lean. The Fanuc angle memory
stayed unknown, so the first tilted feed refused at a stated rotary
rate (tilthead.mch).

- stamp: when a path leans, each station before the first lean states
  the upright Z column; a path that never leans stays silent.
- dump: in a stream that leans, the first move that states the Z
  column commands explicit zero angles. A stream that states no pose
  before its first tilted feed still refuses.

The opening rapid at the clearance now carries A0 B0. The rate guard
is unchanged.

Fixes #3300

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
